{"name":"Ship Steering Wheel","hex":"#62493b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ship","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A water-borne vessel generally larger than a boat.","A vessel which travels through any medium other than across land, such as an airship or spaceship."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send by water-borne transport.","To send (a parcel or container) to a recipient (by any means of transport)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship"},{"term":"steering","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of steer"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Equipment used to control direction; something used to steer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steering"},{"term":"wheel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A circular device capable of rotating on its axis, facilitating movement or transportation or performing labour in machines.\n\n A steering wheel and its implied control of a vehicle.","A steering wheel and its implied control of a vehicle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roll along on wheels.","To transport something or someone using any wheeled mechanism, such as a wheelchair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wheel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steering wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A steering wheel is a type of steering control in vehicles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Steering_wheels_from_different_periods.jpg/330px-Steering_wheels_from_different_periods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steering_wheel","wikidata":"Q679300"},{"title":"Ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ship is a large watercraft designed for travel across the surface of a body of water, carrying cargo or passengers, or in support of specialized tasks such as warfare, oceanography and fishing. Ships are generally distinguished from boats, based on size, shape, load capacity and purpose. Ships have supported exploration, trade, warfare, migration, colonization, and science. Ship transport is responsible for the largest portion of world commerce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg/330px-Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship","wikidata":"Q11446"},{"title":"Steering","blocks":[{"text":"Steering is the control of the direction of motion or the components that enable its control. Steering is achieved through various arrangements, among them ailerons for airplanes, rudders for boats, cylic tilting of rotors for helicopters, and many more."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Jersey_Town_Criterium_2011_81.jpg/330px-Jersey_Town_Criterium_2011_81.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steering","wikidata":"Q18891017"},{"title":"Wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A wheel is a rotating component intended to turn on an axle bearing. The wheel is one of the key components of the wheel and axle, which is one of the six simple machines. Wheels, in conjunction with axles, allow heavy objects to be moved easily, facilitating transportation, supporting loads, and performing work in machines. Wheels are also used for other purposes, such as a ship's wheel, steering wheel, potter's wheel, and flywheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg/330px-Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel","wikidata":"Q446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Gr%C3%A